ing  or hold and i can never understand half  have it i shouldn't say never but a lot  of times it's quite confusing as what  they as to what they want you to do  until you start to hear a few examples  but i never do it i just listen i just  listen and in all of their drills i just  listen to the pattern and i find that  listening to the pattern is much more  powerful than me interjecting  my effort to remember what was in the  sentence and to try to do whatever it is  they ask you to do to i find that a  burden  and and something that's unpleasant to  do in all of the language books that i  use  whenever there are drills or questions i  never do them i may read  the  various sentences which very often you  know highlight a particular pattern or i  might go to the answers and read all of  the answers which highlight a particular  pattern so it's this exposure to a  pattern that i find useful whereas doing  the drills i don't find useful by the  same token the role playing is not  something that i would willingly  participate in because it's not natural  i believe that  listening to interesting stories or even  listening to you know a concentration  concentrated exposure to certain  patterns is gradually increasing the  ability improving the ability of the  brain  to sift through and sort through and  organize this language that ultimately  just as i prefer my listening and  reading to be  on subjects of interest to me  you know i also prefer  my speaking to be on subjects of  interest to me  so that's why i wait until i at least  have some words in the language and some  comprehension  so that now  i can start speaking to someone and i  would rather speak  on a subject of interest rather than  pretending that i am a clerk in a store  or uh you know work at the post office  or whatever it might be  i will ask the person where do you live  he lives in  i don't know a syrian refugee in turkey  how is life in turkey are there many  refugees there from syria what's going  to happen in syria those are the kinds  of discussions that i will have in  arabic and those will be meaningful uh  discussions and so that is an  opportunity for me to practice output to  find out what i'm missing to go back to  my input to work on words and phrases  for the next encounter but the next  encounter with my tutor will again be a  real encounter speaking it won't be a  drill it won't be role playing it won't  be any of these things it'll be  something meaningful to me  so  that's why personally  uh being prompted to say something being  prompted to perform a role  uh  being prompted to respond to drills all  of this is something that i  resist now maybe that's just a personal  preference in fact it's certainly a  personal preference other people you  know have different approaches but i  just wanted to explain  the approach that i take and  let you know that i'm looking forward to  starting to speak in arabic but i don't  want to do it until we have our new  speaking platform at link uh and then  you'll be able to follow my my progress  uh i'm even thinking of  of uh maybe tracking say if i speak  every day  then over a period of a week or so or  two  just tracking my progress  at least for my own purpose so i'll save  a minute of each discussion  and i'll then have at least for my own  purposes a record of my progress as i  start to activate  my arabic learning  okay thank you for listening  bye for now  [Music]  you
 

